Watermarking API

Overview

This project provides an API for embedding and detecting watermarks in audio files. It uses a command-line interface (CLI) tool to process .wav files, ensuring audio integrity while embedding hidden data.

Features


Embed Watermark: Convert a text message into a binary watermark and embed it into an audio file.

Detect Watermark: Scan an audio file for the presence of an embedded watermark and retrieve its content.

Adaptive Processing: Adjusts watermark parameters based on loudness and dominant frequency of the input audio.

Requirements

Python 3.x

FastAPI

FFmpeg, SoX 

Pydub

CLI Binaries: SitMarkAudio2MEmbedderCLI, SitMarkAudio2MDetectorCLI

Installation

pip install fastapi uvicorn pydub numpy scipy

Ensure that FFmpeg and SoX are installed and accessible in your system path.

Usage

Running the Server

uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

API Endpoints

1. Embed Watermark

Endpoint: POST /embed/
Parameters:

audio: Uploaded WAV file

watermark_message: Text message to embed

2. Detect Watermark

Endpoint: POST /detect/
Parameters:

audio: Uploaded WAV file

Response:

message: Success or failure message

detected_watermark: The extracted watermark message (if found)

watermark_length: Length of the detected watermark (in bits)

File Structure

project-folder/
│-- main.py  # FastAPI application
│-- binaries/
│   │-- SitMarkAudio2MEmbedderCLI
│   │-- SitMarkAudio2MDetectorCLI
│-- uploads/  # Processed audio files

